sequenceDiagram
    actor User as Operator
    participant RC as JobsConnectSubcommand
    participant DDB as DynamoDB<br/><prefix>-results
    participant EC2 as AWS EC2
    participant SSM as Session Manager<br/>(ssm, ssmmessages)
    participant PL as session-manager-plugin<br/>(local process)
    participant R as Runner instance<br/>amazon-ssm-agent

    Note over R,SSM: every runner registers its agent at boot (RunnerRole: UpdateInstanceInformation + ssmmessages channels)<br/>no inbound rule, the agent dials out over 443

    rect rgb(240, 248, 255)
        Note over User,R: baas jobs connect <jobId>
        User->>RC: baas jobs connect 20261022T130353548Z-c4baa457
        alt session-manager-plugin not on PATH
            RC-->>User: names the plugin and its install command, exit 1 -- no AWS call at all
        end
        RC->>DDB: Query jobId-index, then GetItem
        alt no job item in this deployment
            RC-->>User: "No job found", exit 1
        end
        RC->>EC2: describeInstances(baas-job-id tag AND baas-deployment, state pending|running)
        alt no live instance (finished, or still reserving)
            RC-->>User: "no pending or running instance (stored status: s)", exit 1
        end
        Note over RC: the instance decides, not the stored status -- a job stuck in launched can be reached
        RC->>SSM: DescribeInstanceInformation(instanceId)
        alt agent not Online yet
            RC-->>User: "not reachable yet ... retry shortly", exit 1
        end
        RC-->>User: "terminates by about HH:MM UTC" -- LaunchTime + watchdogSeconds from the reservation
        RC->>SSM: StartSession(target, DocumentName = prefix-session-runner)
        Note over SSM: operator role: only baas-deployment-tagged instances, only that document<br/>(SessionDocumentAccessCheck), so the account default and port forwarding are denied
        SSM-->>RC: SessionId, StreamUrl, TokenValue
        RC->>PL: exec with the AWS CLI's six arguments -- no credential reaches it
        PL->>SSM: OpenDataChannel(StreamUrl, token)
        SSM->>R: session as ssm-user, cd /app, exec bash
        loop while the plugin runs, every 15 s
            RC->>EC2: describeInstances(instanceId) -- a failed call counts as live
        end
        alt the operator types exit
            PL-->>RC: exit 0 -- RC returns it
        else plugin exits non-zero
            RC->>SSM: TerminateSession -- best effort, the session may still be open
        else instance shutting-down or terminated (job finished, watchdog, terminate)
            RC-->>User: "Instance i-... has terminated, ending the session."
            RC->>SSM: TerminateSession -- the plugin then leaves on its own, or is stopped after 10 s
            RC-->>User: exit 0
        end
        Note over RC,R: a session never delays or extends termination, and nothing about it is recorded
    end
